module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.NaturalTrapsLarge

/-!
# Traps for 22 more blocks of periods 13 and 14, from locked windows of 16 cells, checked in parts

The census of locked windows of 16 cells finds, for every block, the bottom components of its locked windows. At
periods 13 and 14, 22 of the blocks that their chains hold, 10 of period 13 and 12 of period 14, are reached only by
their own components, of 3,169 to 22,746 states, which [CensusTraps13](CensusTraps13.md) and
[CensusTraps14](CensusTraps14.md) leave out. Each is checked here as [NaturalTrapsLarge](NaturalTrapsLarge.md) checks
its trap: the packed numbers in pieces of 65,536 bits, and the check in parts of 1,024 states, one kernel check each.

* `cen<block>`, `cen<block>_<part>`, `cen<block>_parts`, `cen<block>_check`: the traps, their parts, and the check of
  [WordTraps](WordTraps.md) for each.
* `censusTrapsLarge`, `censusTrapsLarge_check`, `censusTrapsLarge_blocks`: the list, its check and its blocks.
* `censusLarge_absorption_excludes`: for each of them, if every finitely supported right half driven by the block
  enters its trap, the center column does not eventually repeat the block.

The traps and their parts come from `python -m computations.lock_chain --lean-census-large`. The natural-language
argument is `CensusTrapsLarge.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata

